// More Rewards rewards file. Add your own end-of-day rewards here, or change the game's.
// Changes apply the next time the game starts, or at once when you save from the Rewards tab in the Mod Manager.
// Delete this file to get the default back.
// The mod's log (BepInEx/more-rewards.log) lists anything in here it could not use, and why.
//
// A reward entry:
//   "id"           the reward's ID. Use a game reward's ID to change it, or a new ID to add one.
//   "enabled"      true or false; a switched-off entry changes nothing, its buffs and effects included
//   "copyFrom"     for a new ID: the game reward it starts from (its icon, look, needs and what it gives)
//   "name", "description"   text, either "plain" or { "en": "...", "zh": "..." }
//   "cost"         survival points to take it
//   "needs"        the rewards you must own first, such as [31271]
//   "furniture"    furniture IDs; it is only offered once you can build one of them
//   "pools"        { "pool ID": weight }: the pools it is drawn from, and how likely next to the others there
//                  (the game uses 1, or 3 for its start-of-run pools 1020, 1021 and 1022)
//   "fields"       any Config_Talent field, such as { "WebIcon": "../../Res/Furniture/UI_Item_Icon_Furnit_M_900300101.png" }.
//                  These apply to every level. "IsReget": true lets it be offered and bought again after you own it,
//                  "EndlessMode": 6 offers it in Endless Mode only (0 is any run), and "PlayerSelectId": [1, 2] gives it
//                  only to those characters (empty is every character).
//   "fromDay"      the first day it can be offered; 0 is from the first day
//   "layers"       with "IsReget": how many times its effect stacks when it is bought again
//   "gives"        [ { "effect": "game:<script>", "fields": { ... } }, ... ]: what it does, up to 10 things, each made
//                  from an effect script the game runs (Buff/<script> in Config_Effect) with your fields.
//                  Left out, it does what its copyFrom does. "mr:wind-power" with { "FloatValue0": 0.15 } makes
//                  Wind Power's turbines make 15% more power. A give can have "levels": [ { fields }, ... ] too,
//                  the fields that change at each level. "give": { ... } with one give works as well.
//   "levels"       [ { "cost", "name", "description", "pools", "fields" }, ... ]: up to 10 levels, like Sunlight
//                  Collection I, II and III. Level 1 is "id", level 2 is "id" + 1, and so on; each level needs the one
//                  below it. Anything a level leaves out is the reward's own value. Left out, the reward has one level.
//                  On a game reward, a list shorter than the game's switches off the game's levels above it.
//   "buffs", "effects"   Config_Buff and Config_Effect rows this reward changes or makes (see below)
//
// A buff or effect entry: "id", an optional "copyFrom" (needed to make a new row), and "fields",
// named as the game's tables name them (ConfigName, IntValue0, FloatValue0, EffectConfigId...).
// The "buffs" and "effects" lists at the bottom always apply.
//
// "days" changes which pools a day draws its rewards from: [ { "day": 57, "pools": [ { "pool": 1020, "amount": 2 }, ... ] } ].
// The game goes down the list in order and draws "amount" rewards from each pool, never the same one twice, then shows
// the first 3, so a pool lower down only shows when the ones above come up short. The day must be one the game's table
// has; after its last day the game keeps using the last one.
//
// With Wind Power 0.9.3 or newer installed, the mod adds Wind Collection I, II and III (39001 to 39003).
// An entry here with one of those IDs replaces them, so you can change them or switch them off.
//
// An example: a cheaper copy of Sunlight Collection I that gives 10% more solar power. To use it, copy it into the
// "rewards" list below without the // at the start of each line.
//    {
//      "id": 39101,
//      "copyFrom": 31271,
//      "name": { "en": "Small Solar Boost", "zh": "小型太阳能增益" },
//      "description": { "en": "Increases solar panel power generation efficiency by 10%.", "zh": "太阳能板产电效率 +10%" },
//      "cost": 5,
//      "pools": { "1013": 1 },
//      "gives": [{ "effect": "game:AE_PowerSolarEfficiency", "fields": { "FloatValue0": 0.1 } }]
//    }
{
  "rewards": [],
  "buffs": [],
  "effects": []
}
